[UTCDate "2021.02.08"]
[UTCTime "16:26:17"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Now we show what happens if White plays an early c4 instead of developing pieces. Play your Caro-Kann. }
1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. c4 Nf6 5. Nf3 { Levy wants you to solidify the center. How can you do that? } 5... e6 6. Nc3 Be7 7. Be2 O-O { Rozman gives you another option here. If you had taken on c4 you force white's bishop to move twice. We'll run through that next. } { [%cal Gd5c4,Ge2c4,Gf1e2] } (7... dxc4 { Also good, make that bishop move twice. }) 8. O-O { Now your plan is to develop your bishop to b7. } { [%cal Gb7b6,Gc8b7] } *


